PATCH 574: the mission-over transition -- 5f64's CF, the two byte-wide flags 0x7b1e/0x87bd, and the
cockpit marker producers c47d/c4a2 with their record writers b4cd/b4a3.

board:0017.  With the meshes loaded (573) the AZER1 self-play reaches DEFEAT; three defects then stood
between the verdict and the debrief, each found by watching the byte it corrupted:

  5f64  the platoon-label phase INIT (c33c's walk INIT calls it every frame) runs 671b for the first
        label group and `jb 5fa9` marks the phase done when there is none.  Ghidra hard-wired that CF
        to false: on the DEFEAT frame every own vehicle is a wreck, 671b finds no group, and 5fb0 then
        runs with [0x7d1c]=0 and a stale [0x7d1e]=0 -- its `dec [0x7d1e] ; jne` never reaches 671b, it
        emits one label record per call for 65536 calls, and its STRSEG:[0x12c7+[0x7c04]] store marches
        128 KB past the label table over the MEMMGR descriptor pool at 0x34020; the per-frame compaction
        096c/0dc2 then walks a zeroed free list for ever (the hang after the verdict).
        (5f83 `movb [0x7d29],0x29` is a byte store; DAT_2000_3d29 is typed as a word.)
  0x87bd  every one of the 26 asm accesses is `mov BYTE [0x87bd],3` (the cockpit damage flash, 60f4 and
        the 506d..5d3d sites); Ghidra typed DAT_2000_47bd as a WORD, so each store zeroed byte[0x87be] =
        the low byte of the cockpit container's child-list offset (record 0x87b8+6, copied by 4823's
        1e27 from template 0x2bed).  With childlo 0x64 -> 0, container node 3b24's children became
        0x3af0..0x3c20 -- its own parent list -- and the first repaint after the player's vehicle was
        hit recursed 20d6/20ea until the stack overflowed (the transition's SIGSEGV).
  0x7b1e  likewise (byte in every access: 47bd/5267/526e/5280/5287/5d1b/5d66/60f4; typed as a word):
        the word store cleared the view flag byte[0x7b1f] that c528 and 1682b test.
  c47d/c4a2  c33c phase handlers 0 and 8, the cockpit-view (byte[0x1549]==0x1e) marker and position-
        sprite producers: their CF was dropped (board:0015) and their record writers 0f69:be3d = b4cd
        and 0f69:be13 = b4a3 received stack residue as the ES:DI record cursor (a host deref of 3460
        on the first cockpit frame after the verdict).  Rebuilt: c47d walks the STRSEG entries
        [0xe6e4]..[0xe6e2] (stride 5, {x, y, colour}) into method-0x12 (37cd pixel) records; c4a2 walks
        the position list [0xe70b] ([0xe709] entries, stride 8) into method-0x10 (3823 sprite 0x1398)
        records; both through g_fist_render_di like the patch-310/526 writers.

After 574 the self-play runs through DEFEAT, e814, the pilot-file save (616e), the statistics update
(6220) and into e4bb's screen without a crash or hang.  What e4bb shows is the command-map template
0x2d1d; the original shows "MISSION LOST / BATTLE STATISTICS ... PRESS ANY KEY TO PROCEED" over a
picture -- ba63 fills those strings into STRSEG:0x41dc.. and the container node 3b24's child list
0x3b54.. is where they are drawn; the port's frame has the map toolbar and no text.  Measured next
(tools/oracle/census_debrief.sh: the original's post-verdict sequence frame by frame).
